      "knowledge_point_id": "908ce57e-7ca8-5e5f-bdcb-0d2ef79f10ea",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Range of Values of a Parameter for Which a Geometric Series Converges",
      "problem": "For which values of $k$ does the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{(\\frac{64}{{2}^{k}})}^{n}$ converge?",
      "worked_solution": "We see that this is a geometric series with a common ratio of $r=\\frac{64}{{2}^{k}}.$ \n\nFor the series to converge, we require $|r|<1.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{64}{{2}^{k}}| & <1 \\\\ \\frac{64}{{2}^{k}} & <1 \\\\ 64 & <{2}^{k} \\\\ {2}^{k} & >64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we could remove the absolute value bars because $\\frac{64}{{2}^{k}}$ is always positive.\n\nThe equation ${2}^{k}=64$ has the solution $k=6.$ Now, since ${2}^{k}$ increases as $k$ increases, the solution to ${2}^{k}>64$ must be $k>6.$",
